                             /home/pst/Documents/vhl/vhl_ana/virtual_hardware_laboratary/ana/resources/bq79616_eval_board.scud:\n     1\t# Circuit Overview &                    
                             Functional Architecture\n     2\t\n     3\tThe schematic represents a high-cell-count Battery Management System (BMS) based on the                  
                             **Texas Instruments BQ79616PAPQ1** Automotive Battery Monitor and Balancer. This IC is capable of monitoring up to 16 series cells.\n               
                             4\t\n     5\tThe design includes:\n     6\t1.  **Main BMS IC (U1):** The BQ79616 handles cell voltage monitoring, internal cell                     
                             balancing, and GPIO-based sensing.\n     7\t2.  **Cell Count Configuration:** A set of jumper resistors (currently DNP) allows the                  
                             system to be configured for fewer than 16 cells by shorting unused upper channels (`CBxx`/`VCxx`) to the highest active potential.\n                
                             8\t3.  **Temperature Sensing Interface:** A bank of 8 thermistor dividers powered by the IC's `TSREF` output. These connect to the IC's             
                             GPIO pins via a configuration header (J4).\n     9\t4.  **Power & Communication:** The IC is powered from the battery stack (`PWR` net)             
                             and generates its own internal rails (`AVDD`, `CVDD`, `DVDD`). It features a daisy-chainable communication interface (`COMH`/`COML`)                
                             and a local UART/SPI interface (`RX`/`TX`).\n    10\t5.  **Auxiliary Measurement Inputs:** The system includes two configurable paths               
                             for driving the `BBP` and `BBN` pins (Pins 64/63) of the BMS IC. These pins are typically used for auxiliary voltage measurements. The              
                             two options are:\n    11\t    *   **Bus Bar Measurement (DNP):** Measures the voltage difference between `BBP_CELL` and `BBN_CELL` via              
                             a differential RC filter.\n    12\t    *   **Current Sense Measurement (Active):** Measures the voltage from `SRP_S` and `SRN_S`                    
                             (likely current sense shunt taps). This path is currently populated (direct connection).\n    13\t6.  **Communication Interface:**\n                
                             14\t    *   **Isolated Interface:** A digital isolator (U2) provides a galvanically isolated UART and Fault interface between the BMS               
                             IC (High Voltage) and an external host/microcontroller (Low Voltage).\n    15\t    *   **Direct Interface:** A header is provided for               
                             direct, non-isolated connection to the BMS UART pins.\n    16\t\n    17\t7.  **NPN Power Supply:** An external NPN transistor circuit               
                             is provided to regulate the `LDOIN` supply for the BMS IC, reducing power dissipation within the IC. This circuit is powered from the               
                             main `PWR` rail.\n    18\t\n    19\t# Components Inventory\n    20\t\n    21\t**Integrated Circuits**\n    22\t*   **U1:** TI                       
                             BQ79616PAPQ1 (16-Channel Battery Monitor)\n    23\t*   **U2:** TI ISO7342CQDWRQ1 (Digital Isolator)\n    24\t\n                                     
                             25\t**Transistors**\n    26\t*   **Q1:** NPN Transistor (External LDO Pass Element). Active.\n    27\t*   **Q2:** NPN Transistor                    
                             footprint. DNP (Do Not Populate).\n    28\t\n    29\t**Power & Decoupling**\n    30\t*   **Input Filter:** R5 (30.0\u03a9), C5 (10nF)               
                             on `BAT` pin.\n    31\t*   **NPN Supply:**\n    32\t    *   **Input Path:** `PWR` connects to Q1 Collector via series resistors R4                  
                             (200\u03a9) and R3 (100\u03a9).\n    33\t    *   **Input Filter:** C1 (0.22\u03bcF) on the Collector of Q1.\n    34\t    *                          
                             **Regulation:** Q1 Emitter drives `LDOIN`. Q1 Base is driven directly by `NPNB`.\n    35\t*   **Internal Regulators:**\n    36\t    *               
                             **AVDD/CVDD/DVDD:** Decoupled by C6 (1\u03bcF), C9 (1\u03bcF), C7 (4.7\u03bcF), C8 (1\u03bcF).\n    37\t    *   **LDOIN:** C59                      
                             (0.1\u03bcF).\n    38\t    *   **NEG5V:** C3 (0.1\u03bcF).\n    39\t    *   **TSREF:** C2 (1\u03bcF).\n    40\t    *   **Isolator                   
                             Power:** C57 (0.1\u03bcF) on `USB2ANY_3.3V`, C58 (0.1\u03bcF) on `CVDD_CO`.\n    41\t*   **Indicator:** Green LED D1 with R121 (1.0k)               
                             and Jumper J6 (Power Indicator).\n    42\t\n    43\t**Resistors (Configuration Jumpers)**\n    44\t*   **Type:** 0-ohm links\n    45\t*             
                             **Status:** All currently marked DNP (Do Not Populate)\n    46\t*   **Designators:**\n    47\t    *   **CB Series:** R21, R22, R25,                 
                             R26\n    48\t    *   **VC Series:** R23, R24, R27, R28\n    49\t    *   **Auxiliary Select:** R10, R13, R17 (DNP).\n    50\t\n                      
                             51\t**Auxiliary Measurement Components**\n    52\t*   **Bus Bar Filter:**\n    53\t    *   **Resistors:** R9, R12 (402\u03a9)\n    54\t             
