                             **C60:** 1uF Capacitor\n    84\t    *   **D3:** 24V Dual Zener/TVS Diode\n    85\t*   **DNP Components:** R20 (100k), C12 (DNP) on RT8              
                             channel.\n    86\t\n    87\t# Connectivity & Signal Flow\n    88\t\n    89\t**Main IC (U1) Connections:**\n    90\t*   **Cell Inputs:**             
                             `VC0` through `VC16` connect to the cell voltage sense lines.\n    91\t*   **Balancing:** `CB0` through `CB16` connect to the cell                  
                             balance lines.\n    92\t*   **GPIOs:** `GPIO1` through `GPIO8` connect to the temperature sensing block (via J4).\n    93\t*   **Power              
                             Supply:**\n    94\t    *   `BAT` (Pin 1) is the high-voltage supply, filtered from the `PWR` net.\n    95\t    *   `AVDD`, `CVDD`,                  
                             `DVDD` are internal regulator outputs tied together and decoupled to GND.\n    96\t    *   `TSREF` (Pin 51) provides the reference                  
                             voltage for the thermistors.\n    97\t    *   `LDOIN` (Pin 47), `NEG5V` (Pin 44), `NPNB` (Pin 48), `REFHP` (Pin 37) are additional                  
                             regulator/reference pins.\n    98\t    *   **NPN Supply (Optional):** `LDOIN` is powered via an external NPN (Q1). `PWR` -> R4 -> R3 ->             
                             Q1(C). Q1(E) -> `LDOIN`. Base is driven by `NPNB`. C1 filters the Collector input.\n    99\t*   **Communication:**\n   100\t    *                   
                             **Daisy Chain:** `COMHP`/`COMHN` (High side) and `COMLP`/`COMLN` (Low side) for stacking multiple BMS ICs.\n   101\t    *   **Local                 
                             Host:** `RX` (Pin 52) and `TX` (Pin 53) for communication with a microcontroller.\n   102\t    *   **Fault:** `NFAULT` (Pin 62) is an               
                             active-low fault output.\n   103\t*   **Grounding:**\n   104\t    *   `AVSS`, `CVSS`, `DVSS`, `REFHM`, and `PAD` are tied to the local              
                             GND.\n   105\t    *   **System Grounding:** A note specifies that \"GND is tied to CELL0 at connector via a thick trace,\" establishing             
                             the reference potential for the low-voltage side.\n   106\t\n   107\t**Communication Interface Details:**\n   108\t*   **Isolated Path              
                             (via U2):**\n   109\t    *   **TX (MCU -> BMS):** `USB2ANY_TX_3.3` (J17-7) -> U2 (INB->OUTB) -> `RX_CO` -> J21 -> `RX` (U1-52).\n                   
                             110\t    *   **RX (BMS -> MCU):** `TX` (U1-53) -> U2 (INC->OUTC) -> `USB2ANY_RX_3.3` (J17-8).\n   111\t    *   **Fault (BMS -> MCU):**              
                             `NFAULT` (U1-62) -> J2 -> `NF_J` -> U2 (IND->OUTD) -> `NFAULT_C` (J17-3).\n   112\t    *   **Power:** U2 Isolated side powered by                   
                             `USB2ANY_3.3V`. BMS side powered by `CVDD` via J18.\n   113\t*   **Direct Path (Non-Isolated):**\n   114\t    *   **J3 (Direct UART                 
                             Header):**\n   115\t        *   Pin 1: GND.\n   116\t        *   Pin 2: `NFAULT` (Schematic) / \"FAULTn\" (Text).\n   117\t        *                
                             Pin 3: `RX_C` (Schematic) / \"RX\" (Text).\n   118\t        *   Pin 4: `TX` (Schematic) / \"TX\" (Text).\n   119\t        *                         
                             **Conflict:** The text description for J3 pins 4 and 5 (\"4 RX\", \"5 TX\") contradicts the schematic wires (Pin 4 is `TX`, Pin 3 is                
                             `RX_C`). The schematic wires are assumed correct: Pin 3 is Input (RX), Pin 4 is Output (TX).\n   120\t    *   `RX` (BMS) can be driven              
                             from `RX_C` (J3-3) via R119 (100\u03a9) and J1.\n   121\t    *   `TX` (BMS) connects directly to J3-4.\n   122\t\n   123\t**Auxiliary               
                             Measurement Inputs (BBP/BBN):**\n   124\t*   **Pins:** `BBP` (Pin 64) and `BBN` (Pin 63) on U1.\n   125\t*   **Path 1 (Bus Bar -                    
                             DNP):**\n   126\t    *   Inputs: `BBP_CELL` and `BBN_CELL`.\n   127\t    *   Filtering: Differential RC filter formed by R9/R12                     
                             (402\u03a9) and C10 (0.47\u03bcF).\n   128\t    *   Connection: Connects to `BBP`/`BBN` via R10/R13 (0\u03a9). Currently DNP.\n                     
                             129\t*   **Path 2 (Current Sense - Active):**\n   130\t    *   Inputs: `SRP_S` and `SRN_S`.\n   131\t    *   Filtering: Optional C11                
