                             resistors are DNP, Path 2 is the active source.\n   134\t\n   135\t**Cell Balance (CB) Configuration Path:**\n   136\t*   **R25**                   
                             connects `CB12` to `CB13`\n   137\t*   **R21** connects `CB13` to `CB14`\n   138\t*   **R26** connects `CB14` to `CB15`\n   139\t*                  
                             **R22** connects `CB15` to `CB16`\n   140\t\n   141\t**Voltage Sense (VC) Configuration Path:**\n   142\t*   **R27** connects `VC12` to             
                             `VC13`\n   143\t*   **R23** connects `VC13` to `VC14`\n   144\t*   **R28** connects `VC14` to `VC15`\n   145\t*   **R24** connects                  
                             `VC15` to `VC16`\n   146\t\n   147\tIn the current DNP state, all these lines (`CB12`-`CB16` and `VC12`-`VC16`) are electrically                    
                             isolated from each other within this specific block.\n   148\t\n   149\t**Temperature Measurement Subsystem:**\n   150\t*   **Reference             
                             Power:** `TSREF` (Thermistor Reference) connects to the `PULLUP` rail via jumper **J5**.\n   151\t*   **Divider Network:** The `PULLUP`             
                             rail feeds 8 parallel voltage dividers. Each divider consists of a 10.0k top resistor (e.g., R7) and a bottom NTC thermistor (e.g.,                 
